+/// A SleighArchitecture keeps one translator per language and resets and initializes it
+/// for each new Architecture of that language, which leaves an earlier Architecture still in
+/// use decoding through the new one's load image and context. This points the translator back
+/// at the given load image and context database, which initialize() has already registered
+/// the context variables with, as reset() and initialize() would for a new one.
+/// (decompiler-js patch, not upstream)
+/// \param ld is the load image of the program returned to
+/// \param c_db is the context database of the program returned to
+void Sleigh::resume(LoadImage *ld,ContextDatabase *c_db)
+
+{
+  reset(ld,c_db);
+  buildDisassemblyCache();
+}
